From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 20:17:52 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 001/207] deepseek: build CPU asset generators before CUDA
 images

Install the token-map exporter and the real AOT planner without booting a CUDA model. Parse complete release metadata for CPU preparation while retaining checkpoint representation refusals in serving.

Host checks cover CLI admission and the public 1017 config. The second node CPU qualification passes formatting, zero new lean identities, native/plain builds, the full host and CUDA subsets, kernel contracts, security, golden, fuzz and CI tool checks. Actual metadata produces the canonical token map and the reference generators produce RoPE, signatures, needs and an SM121 cubin.
